`orderPatterns(patterns)` validates and ranks route patterns. A valid pattern starts with `/`, has no empty segments, and each segment is either a static sequence of ASCII letters, digits, `_`, or `-`, or a parameter beginning with `:` followed by one or more ASCII letters, digits, or `_`. `/` is valid and has zero segments. Invalid patterns throw `Error("invalid pattern")` before any output is returned.

Rank patterns by descending number of static segments, then descending total segment count. Ties must preserve original input order. Duplicate strings remain as separate entries in their original relative order. The function must not mutate or retain the input array, and its output must be a new array. An empty input returns an empty array.

Known-bad source:

```typescript
export function orderPatterns(patterns: string[]): string[] {
  const validSegment = /^(?:[A-Za-z0-9_-]+|:[A-Za-z0-9_]+)$/;
  const ranked = patterns.map((pattern, index) => {
    if (!pattern.startsWith("/")) throw new Error("invalid pattern");
    const segments = pattern === "/" ? [] : pattern.slice(1).split("/");
    if (segments.some((segment) => !validSegment.test(segment))) {
      throw new Error("invalid pattern");
    }
    const staticCount = segments.filter((segment) => !segment.startsWith(":" мен)).length;
    return { pattern, index, staticCount, segmentCount: segments.length };
  });
  ranked.sort((a, b) =>
    b.staticCount - a.staticCount ||
    b.segmentCount - a.segmentCount ||
    b.index - a.index
  );
  return ranked.map((entry) => entry.pattern);
}
```

